  "slug": "artist:obituary",
  "name": "Obituary",
  "editorial_article": "Formed in Tampa in 1984 as Executioner, Obituary helped define the Florida death metal sound by favoring sluggish, doom-inspired tempos over the thrash-influenced speed favored by their peers. The band, anchored by brothers John and Donald Tardy, built their reputation on heavy, groove-oriented guitar riffs and John Tardy’s distinctive, primal growls. Their 1990 sophomore album, Cause of Death, remains a pivotal entry in the genre, featuring lead guitarist James Murphy. In the mid-90s, they explored broader sonic territory; their 1997 album Back from the Dead incorporated elements of hardcore punk and, on the track 'Bullituary', even experimented with rap-metal. Following a hiatus from 1998 to 2003, the band returned with 2005's Frozen in Time and later relied on a successful 2013 Kickstarter campaign to self-release Inked in Blood before partnering with Relapse Records. Current bassist Terry Butler joined the lineup in 2010, contributing to the band's persistent output of crushing, death-metal-centric studio albums.",
